        "original_id": "0beb58a8-1808-56ad-a737-bb4d9686ffbe",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Swallow Bluff Island Mounds, Saltillo, Tennessee River, Hardin County, Tennessee, eastern Tennessee, northern Alabama\n- Topics: Mississippian culture, archaeological sites, Cherokee territorial history, river names\n\nFacts:\n- The Swallow Bluff Island Mounds is a Mississippian culture archaeological site identified as 40HR16.\n- The Swallow Bluff Island Mounds is located near Saltillo on an island in the Tennessee River in Hardin County, Tennessee.\n- The Tennessee River was once popularly known as the Cherokee River, among other names.\n- Many Cherokee had territory along the banks of the Tennessee River, especially in eastern Tennessee and northern Alabama.",
